{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1194108-so-what-s-the-talassii-anathema","id":1194108,"title":"So what's the Talassii Anathema?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-10T18:17:07-08:00","id":1194108,"title":"So what's the Talassii Anathema?","content":"After reading through the Player's Guide, I find I can't explictly figure out what the Anathema they all suffer is supposed to be. Most of the text is written as if the Hero simply gave them a persistent bad reputation. But then the &quot;Playing a Talassii&quot; section on page 48 has this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One common trait occurs among nearly all Talassii: No matter how their Horrors appear, they exude an air of menace. It starts out as a low-grade feeling of discomfort, which a victim can easily dismiss in most cases. However, when a Talassii manifests his Horror through Atavisms or spends enough time with a victim to manifest his Birthright, the aura of malicious intent comes to its full fruition, contributing to any terror or weakness the victim experiences. The Captor\u2019s actual intent in such manifestations matters little, even in self-defense; any given victim immediately assumes that the Captor is out to get him, personally<br /> ...Out of all the Families under the Dark Mother, the Talassii arguably have the least impetus to continue their story for any longer than it has to go. Their curse puts them at a disadvantage among Beasts, many supernatural creatures, and any mortals who see their Atavisms. </div> </div> </div>So is this &quot;air of menace&quot; the real Anathema, or the rape rumors? Did the former cause the latter? And if the &quot;air of menace&quot; is an Anathema-like effect, what kind of mechanical effect would you give that, if any?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T18:34:22-08:00","id":1194112,"title":"","content":"Currently, it's straight up the burden of the name. TO be named Talassii is to be named something vicious and vile, even among the Eldest, and it's a name you can't escape.<br /> <br /> Like, it's being named Craven. What the fuck did your ancestors do that was so bad that they earned that, and why haven't <i>you</i> shed it?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Better examples for the modern day-It's like being named Trump, Weinstein, or Hitler in today's climate.<br /> <br /> EDIT: At least, that's how I read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-10-2018, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T20:04:04-08:00","id":1194123,"title":"","content":"I actually asked about this! The response was that it's basically a stain on their reputation. It's not so much there's any hard mechanical effect; just that when people hear &quot;Talassii,&quot; they think &quot;rapists and kidnappers.&quot; And no matter how any individual Captor works to break that reputation, it just <i>sticks</i>.<br /> <br /> So in game terms it's probably about the Storyteller playing up NPC responses to finding out a PC is a Talassii. (or describing every Talassii NPC as coming across as a creep, even if they don't actually <i>do</i> anything creepy)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}